Not bundled
-----------
- Native Python tooling (native/, the pinned PyPI packages in
  native/uv.lock) is distributed as source plus lockfile and executed
  locally; it is not shipped as built artifacts. The third-party wheels
  prepared for the native bundle are hashed from the frozen lock and their
  license texts are indexed under release/notices/ (see
  docs/distribution/README.md). License declarations are also recorded in
  the inventory and the attribution ledger (docs/ATTRIBUTION.md).
- Development-only tooling (Playwright, Vite, TypeScript, oxlint/oxfmt,
  wrangler, pytest, ajv) is never distributed to end users.
- No experiment-derived assets are included: the T41–T45 experiment
  candidates were rejected or withdrawn from main and are absent from this
  distribution (verified by the inventory: no ONNX/RapidOCR model files,
  no secondary-reader code).

